# Scripts that the packing and publishing jobs run, and the files those scripts import or call. A change to any of
# them also needs a clean Codex security review (PROC-0001, "Review policy, 2026-11-01"). review-gate reads this
# file from main, or from a PR's base branch when a ruleset requires pull requests there.
# One path per line; a path ending in / covers a folder.
#
# Only the publish jobs hold write scopes, and they build nothing: they re-verify, attest and push the bytes the
# read-only stage and pack-libraries jobs made. Those bytes ship as they are, so what makes them is still risky even
# though those jobs run read-only. Product code and dependencies are not listed; they no longer run with the token.
#
# Keep it current: a PR that adds a script to those jobs adds it here.
# review-gate.sh itself counts Directory.Build.props, Directory.Build.targets and Directory.Packages.props at any
# depth. This file is under .github/, so changing it is itself risky.

# release-platform.yml (stage, then publish with contents, id-token, attestations: write)
# validate.yml (pack-libraries, then publish-libraries with packages, id-token, attestations: write)
tooling/fetch-nuget-package.mjs
tooling/gate-contract.mjs
tooling/library-promotion-proof.mjs
